{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779717726,"nonce":"RYrQGglAIjWCL7pBx+R1JsJIimI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDULhPQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/170","origin":"github"},"title":"Configure nav2 Collision Monitor for BizzyBoat (reflex safety layer)","message":"## Context\nPart of standing up an independent reflex safety layer for BizzyBoat (analysis in #169). The perception adapter that turns forward-OAK segmentation into a Collision-Monitor sensor source is tracked in rolker/unh_marine_perception#17.\n\n## Goal\nAdd and configure `nav2_collision_monitor` in BizzyBoat's nav2 bringup (`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`) as an emergency stop/slow layer on the autonomous `cmd_vel` path, **before the mavros setpoint**, fed by the adapter node's output.\n\n## Scope\n- `cmd_vel_in_topic` = controller output; `cmd_vel_out_topic` placed ahead of the mavros setpoint so it gates all autonomous commands (the RC-direct-to-FCU manual path is untouched — correct scope).\n- Source = adapter output (rolker/unh_marine_perception#17).\n- Polygons tuned for boat momentum: favor **slowdown/limit** over hard **stop**, with realistic standoff distance; forward danger zone (single forward camera).\n- Verify in sim before field.\n\n## Caveats\n- Logic/latency-independent of the costmap, but shares the segmentation root + static camera-extrinsic projection.\n- Forward-arc coverage only.\n\n## References\n- #169 (motivating analysis); adapter: rolker/unh_marine_perception#17\n\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}